WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
We seek refuge in God from Satan.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Tonight, we're starting at Sura 54,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.000
55, excuse me.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
And our teacher tonight will be Laurie, right?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
But before we start, I want to make some corrections.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
In my Khutba today, I make some boo-boos sometimes.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Sometimes I say things that appear to be not very tactful.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
For example, we have here a great team of cake-bringers or cake-makers.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
And when I asked, then Rahima was... it was Rahima's turn, Laurie's turn, I said "the best."

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
So, this... they're all, they're all great makers of cakes, bringers of cakes.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
And this appears not to be tactful, but I have to explain to you that each believer is the best.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
So, when I, when I say "the best," I'm referring to every single one of them.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Because we're all...

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.000
I hope I don't make it worse.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:18.000
No, honest, I, because you people are so special that every one of you is the best.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:29.000
And when I say that, I just want to pay you the highest possible compliment without infringing on the others' properties.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
But they all are the best, each one of them.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Every single...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Did I describe your cake as the best when you brought it in?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Now how do I get out of this one?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Help!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
I think I'll get out by saying "okay, take it over, Laurie."

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Laurie: أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.000
I take refuge in God from Satan the rejected.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.000
[55:1] GOD, Most Gracious. [55:2] The One who teaches the Quran.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
[55:3] The One who created the human beings.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
[55:4] The One who taught him how to distinguish right from wrong.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
[55:5] The sun and the moon created his timing devices

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
[55:6] The stars and the trees prostrate.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.000
[55:7] He raised the heaven and established the balance.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.000
[55:8] You shall not transgress when you weigh.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.000
[55:9] You shall be equitable when you weigh; do not cheat when you trade.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
[55:10] He made the earth for all the people.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.000
[55:11] With fruits, and palms sheath.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
[55:12] With food grains and flowers.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.000
[55:13] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.000
[55:14] He created the human from clay, like the potter's.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.000
[55:15] And created the jinns from blazing fire.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
[55:16] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
[55:17] Lord of the two easts and the two wests.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.000
[55:18] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.000
[55:19] He separates the fresh water from the salt water.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.000
[55:20] Between them is a barrier they cannot surmount.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.000
[55:21] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.000
[55:22] From the two seas you extract pearls and coral.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
[55:23] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
[55:24] He controls the ships that roam the sea like flags.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
[55:25] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.000
[55:26] Everyone on earth will perish.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.000
[55:27] But the presence of your Lord will continue. He is the Possessor of Majesty and Honor.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
[55:28] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.000
[55:29] Everyone in the heavens and the earth implores Him. Every day He is in full control.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
[55:30] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.000
[55:31] We will deal with both of you, the two entities, humans and jinns.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.000
[55:32] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:14.000
[55:33] O you jinns and humans, if you can penetrate the outer limits of the heavens and the earth, then penetrate. You can only penetrate when given authority.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.000
[55:34] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:23.000
[55:35] You will be bombarded with masses of fire and molten metal, and you can never succeed.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
[55:36] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: Are you checking the tape, David?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.000
This is why we should be checking them.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Do the same thing over there.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
(unintelligible) has grown up enough now.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Take good care of him.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Laurie: This chapter is very special to me, because I have this weakness that I'm very impatient

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.000
with knowledge, and if I don't know something, I can't grasp it.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.000
And it always caused me trouble in school, because if I didn't understand it, I couldn't do anything about it.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:09.000
And I became Muslim, and I read the Quran, and I found out that I had to submit, even though I didn't understand something.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.000
It was really a test for me, because I just wanted to know.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.000
And I never understood the jinns. I wish like... And I read it and I knew that they...

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Thank you.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:27.000
And I knew because it was in the Quran. I had to believe it, but I didn't know what they were, and nobody could explain it to me.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.000
You know, and I got really wild explanations of what the jinns were.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.000
And it always troubled me, but I just forced myself to submit.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
And in the second chapter of the Quran, where it says that

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
"the believers are those who believe in the unseen." And this was part of the unseen.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:52.000
And I knew that, IN SHAA ALLAH, over time, that God would explain it to me.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:58.000
And one of the blessings of being in this mosque is having things explained to us.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:07.000
And as Rashad said in the Khutba today, it's a mercy from God that He sends a messenger from among us to explain to us.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.000
The knowledge is here in the Quran, and all of us have read the Quran.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.000
You know, I read it once a month, from front to back.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.000
And every time there's something new.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:22.000
And we get what we need at the time we need it.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.000
And we in this mosque are just developing so far. It's just amazing.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:32.000
You know, Rashad and Lisa and Hasan went to Canada, and there were the people believed they way we do.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:39.000
They're still way behind us in the knowledge, because we're here every Friday night, learning and studying.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.000
We have the input of all these believers here.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:47.000
And we have a messenger that is given the knowledge that is passed on to us.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.000
And we're responsible for the information in the Quran.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:57.000
And, you know, the verse in the Quran that was admonishing the (unintelligible), saying that

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:02.000
they were believers when they weren't really. They were just submitters, and that's the first step.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.000
But only the believers can attain Paradise.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:11.000
So, if we don't have absolute certainty, we can't ever grow and develop to our fullest extent.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:15.000
And that's where the increased knowledge is that should bless me.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.000
And I read, you know, I've read this verse so many times, and the first time I read it,

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.000
you too, the humans and the jinns, you know, I just didn't understand what it meant.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:30.000
I didn't understand what the jinns were, what their role was, what they had to do with me or with us.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:37.000
It was just a mystery. And I just, you know, like I said, I had to force myself not to question it, not to be hung up about it.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:43.000
When we had that discussion about jinns in the Quranic studies, I just kept my mouth shut, you know, very different things.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:52.000
But now, just in this last year, we found out what this is, and so this chapter has a totally different meaning.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:56.000
And for the first time, I understand what it means.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:02.000
And we know now that the jinns are, you know, they have the same requirements.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
There's other verses in the Quran that they have the same requirements that we do.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Some of them believed in Jesus, and they believed in other things, and then they heard the Quran,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:16.000
and they believed, and, you know, they have the same requirements that we do.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.000
And they also have the same rewards that we do.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:25.000
You know, there are entities that we can't see. You know, we don't know. They can see us, but we can't see them.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.000
And yet, the Heaven that's described here in later verses is for them, too.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
They have their own, but it's the same set-up as ours. It's exactly the same for them.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Like, you know, these creatures that are so important in this scripture that we don't know anything about.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:48.000
And now we know that the jinns were those that, before creation, sided with Satan and

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:56.000
took a stand against God and believed that Satan could be a god besides God, that God could have partners, which is the ultimate blasphemy.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:02.000
And they were banished, and they have a chance to redeem themselves as well.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:08.000
And our job is to, you know, and I used to read about Satan and his troops

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:13.000
and generations of jinns and humans, that I didn't know, how do they, how do they come to be generations?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:18.000
How do they multiply? How do they, you know, what do they do to reproduce themselves?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Now we know that a jinn is assigned to each one of us, and so their reproduction is,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:31.000
it coincides with our reproduction, that each one of us is given a companion at

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:37.000
the time of our entry into this world, and we're in the same boat. We both sinned.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.000
We both came to this earth with original sin.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:47.000
We both took a stand against God, the jinns more forcefully than we did, but we took the same stand

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.000
as not being for God, because there's only two ways.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.000
Either you're for or you're against, and we were wishy-washy, but basically we were against God.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.000
We've both been given the chance to redeem ourselves.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:07.000
Thing is, the jinns took the definite stand. So, they're going to try to convert us to Satan's way of thinking and to the original sin that we committed.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.000
So, we have to convert them.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:18.000
So from the time of birth, we're in this constant struggle with our jinn companion to convert them to righteousness

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.000
and to protect ourselves from falling into the path of the jinn.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:27.000
And It's a struggle. It's a struggle every day of our lives, and it just goes on and on.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:34.000
And the blessing about knowing who your enemy is, is knowing what they are, what their goal is,

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.000
what their tactics are, so you can learn how to defend yourself.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:41.000
And that's what the Quran is, and that's where these blessings come from.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.000
So, we know that.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:48.000
And to me, the greatest blessing of all is knowing that we do have original sin and we're bad.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:52.000
You know, we were born bad, because we took the stand against God.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.000
So now that we know that, we know what we have to do.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:02.000
We have to, just every day of our lives, try to redeem ourselves from that sin.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:09.000
And the Quran is very specific about giving us the way to do it, and we know now,

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:15.000
we've heard it several times in Khutbas, that we have to ask ourselves every day "who is my god this week?"

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:22.000
Ok. Because that's our only goal in life, is to redeem ourselves. Nothing else has any importance whatsoever.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:28.000
And we have to do certain things. We have to support ourselves. We have to take care of ourselves. But

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:36.000
with the goal in mind that this is to do righteousness, you know, we can't be a burden to society, we can't steal, so we have to work and support ourselves.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:42.000
So, it's all in tune with the same thing, which is purifying ourselves, and growing and developing our souls.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:48.000
So as soon as you take that stand, then the jinns are going to try to,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.000
your companion and others are going to try and make you stray away from that path.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:12:00.000
And the greater the stand you take, the greater the enticements are going to be, and you just have to be prepared.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.000
And I've talked to several people who've said that they've encountered the same thing I

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:09.000
did when I made the stand, that I was going to really try and devote more of my thoughts

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:13.000
to God because I wasn't doing enough, and I knew it, that they just took over,

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:19.000
and they didn't want me to, even the little that I was doing was in danger of not being done at all.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.000
It's just a constant struggle.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:30.000
And so I know this now, and I know that I have to just be on the alert at all times for, for this. And we know that

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.000
most of it is sneaky whispering. And there's even a Sura where, you know, this is

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:42.000
devoted to this, that Satan whispers to us, I mean, little things that don't seem so bad.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.000
You know, we've talked about this before. "Oh, you can wait until the game is over before you pray" or

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.000
you know "I'll pray later," and then something happens and you don't pray.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:54.000
And that time can never be regained. Once you miss the Prayer, you can't make it up. That time is...

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.000
The inhabitants of Hell are the farthest from God on the Day of Judgment.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Knowing that Heaven is close to God, they will leave Hell and sneak into the area closer to God,

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:08.000
but because they are not sufficiently prepared to come close to God,

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.000
they will suffer terribly in the presence of God and will flee back to Hell and so on forever.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Here's this vicious circle that they're in.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.000
A man: It's just like the Jehovah's Witnesses now.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:27.000
They don't believe in Hell, but they believe 144,000 go to Heaven and the remainder

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:33.000
of their chosen people or whatever go to Paradise. But they still deny Hell.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:40.000
They say "there's no burning Hell. There's no none of this. You just no longer exist,"

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:48.000
which is a lie of... outright lying itself, because nothing that exists can be destroyed.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:56.000
You know, like matter can't be created or destroyed, ever destroyed. It just recycles.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:02.000
In the real world that we're in. No, in the other world, this is not the real world, but in the world we're in now.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:10.000
So, they don't believe in Hell, because if you tell them anything contrary to anything pleasant after death,

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:14.000
they say "well, we just don't exist anymore."

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.000
"Well, we never get punished for what we do wrong."

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.000
"And that's our punishment, not existing."

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.000
"Well, we can get a reward. If we're real good, we get this reward."

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.000
"But if we're real bad, we just don't exist anymore."

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.000
"Just have a reward and no punishment."

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: They wish, they wish this.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
A man: That's what I'm saying. This, this is... A woman: Thank you.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Quran...

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.000
A man: This is what I thought about it. Dr. Khalifa: The Quran says 'they will wish that they..."

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.000
A man: Yeah. "This is the Hell they used to deny." Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.000
A man: They deny Hell. Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: I just wanna add here something that we should all know.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.000
I know Laurie knows that but she just didn't mention it yet.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.000
It has to do with the looks.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.000
See, verse 40 says, (unintelligible), number 39.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.000
Where's the...

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.000
Well, not they ask...Oh, 39, yeah.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:14.000
"The humans and the jinn will not be asked about their sins."

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:21.000
Nobody will need to ask anybody about anything, because the believers develop their souls,

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.000
and the disbelievers fail to develop their souls.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:30.000
And in Sura 17, we're told that the differences in the Hereafter are...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.000
In this room, the differences in our sizes are within a few inches.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:41.000
But in the Hereafter, the difference will be like the difference between a mouse and the city of New York, city of Tucson, let's say.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:50.000
So, when you see somebody the size of the city of Tucson, he or she has developed the soul sufficiently.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.000
This is why they will be able to come closer to God.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:58.000
When you see somebody's the size of a mouse, you don't need to ask, you know "what did you do wrong?"

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:04.000
So, that is, this is why nobody will need to ask anybody about their sins.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.000
It is so obvious.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.000
There'll be no question.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:15.000
Also, in Sura 17, we're told that everybody will be the judge for him or herself, to herself.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:24.000
Because in that dimension, we will see what we really look like, how much we really developed or how much we lacked development.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:31.000
So, only ones that are guilty will be recognized by their looks.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:37.000
They'll be undeveloped. They'll be shrunken, like being born without arms and legs.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.000
Deformed.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:45.000
They will be born into the Hereafter, deformed, undeveloped, aborted.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.000
But they'll be alive, very well, I mean, well, very alive, not well.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Also, God lets us understand, as Lori explained in verse 44, how they will try to sneak into Heaven, and they'll find it worse than Hell.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:18.000
They will sneak into the Lower Heaven, and they will find it worse than Hell, because they cannot stand, come any closer to God.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.000
See, God left it completely up to us, completely.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:26.000
This is why God does not inflict an atom's weight of injustice.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.000
It's absolutely up to you.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:35.000
You can be as close to God as you want, in the High Heaven, or you can be as far from God as you want.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.000
It's completely up to us.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.000
So, the conclusion is that God does not put a single person in Hell.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:49.000
It is the people who insist or choose, and they insist on going to Hell.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.000
This, the whole thing will be automatic in the Hereafter.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:58.000
This is why it is important to do, for example, the five Prayers a day.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:02.000
You don't do the five Prayers every day, you are in trouble.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.000
That's the minimum that you can do.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Because those are the meals for the real person.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:16.000
Imagine if you don't feel... your body does not dry, and you don't feed your body for two months.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.000
What will your body look like?

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.000
There's no death in the Hereafter.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.000
Just imagine not eating for two months.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:32.000
And the people out there in the street, they don't feed their soul for years and years and years.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.000
And imagine what they look like. Can you imagine what they look like?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Just look into our dimension here and think of bodies that didn't eat for years.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:52.000
You see those skeletal pictures of the starving people in Central Africa, Ethiopia, Sudan.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.000
What they look like, you can see their ribs.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.000
The shrunk skin and bones.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:05.000
And this happens to the soul if the soul is not fed the five meals every day.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.000
[55:41] The guilty will be recognized by their looks;...

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.000
You can tell who is starving in Africa and who is not.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.000
By looking at them.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:27.000
And in the Hereafter, you will be able to know who is starving and who is not.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Except it will be by choice.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:35.000
So, now we go back to Lori and number 46, The Higher Heaven.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.000
Lori: Yes.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:43.000
[55:46] For those who reverence the glory of their Lord, there will be two Paradises.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.000
[55:47] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.000
[55:48] With abundant vegetation.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.000
[55:49] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.000
[55:50] Two springs run freely therein.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.000
[55:51] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.000
[55:52] They will have two kinds of every fruit.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
[55:53] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:06.000
[55:54] They will relax on furnishings lined with silk while the fruits of the two gardens are brought near.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.000
[55:55] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:14.000
[55:56] They will have magnificent spouses therein, never before touched by any human or jinn.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.000
[55:57] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.000
[55:58] They will look like gems and coral.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.000
[55:59] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:26.000
[55:60] Is the reward of righteousness anything but the best blessing?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.000
[55:61] Which of your Lord's marvels can you two deny?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.000
These verses are just so beautiful.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:38.000
The Higher Heaven, and we know that the verses describing Heaven and Hell are allegorical

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:43.000
because there's no way that we can conceive or understand what it really will be like

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:46.000
until God gives us these things that brings it into our own dimension.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.000
But we know that there are stratifications.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.000
And for those, very clear here,

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.000
[55:46] For those who reverence the glory of their Lord,...

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:01.000
who've done everything that they have been able to do, developed their souls,

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:07.000
who have kept the commandments, who have not set up another god besides God, then God rewards

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.000
those with the best blessings.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.000
And He doesn't even have to do it.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:16.000
But there's a verse in Quran that says that God is appreciative.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.000
And it's just, that's so incredible to me because He doesn't need us at all.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.000
Why should He be appreciative of anything that we do?

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.000
It's just that He is Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:32.000
And we can't comprehend. We can't comprehend that kind of mercy because we're bound by our own

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:41.000
selfishness and, you know, our own desire to succeed and our own concern with our own well-being.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:48.000
We can't imagine that something could be so gracious and so merciful that it could just provide all these things for us.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:54.000
I mean, it's just the ultimate of just leisure, not having to do anything

00:21:54.000 --> 00:22:00.000
and everything that you want, every kind of food that you want to eat, and you don't have to do anything.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.000
It's just, you know, the springs, they're running freely and you don't have to worry about

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.000
finding a spouse and going through all these changes.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:11.000
And you know, they're just there and you don't have to do anything at all.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:16.000
It's just, it's just an incredible mercy.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:19.000
And, you know, what did we have to do in this life to get there?

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:24.000
I mean, it's like the most incredible, you know, if somebody offered you a deal and said

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:30.000
"if you, you know, buy stock at, you know, 50 cents a share and in 10 years, it'll sell for a million dollars a share"

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.000
and you think, you know, that's impossible. How could anything like that exist?

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.000
But this is even greater.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:43.000
All we had to do was say our five Prayers every day, not to have any other gods besides God, but just for our own benefit anyway.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
God doesn't need us.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.000
You know, to do the religious duties that are so simple, to fast for one month,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:56.000
which if we know is good for us, it lowers our blood pressure, it, you know, gives our kidneys a break.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.000
We know that praying is good for us.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.000
You know, we know about lubricating the joints, and combating arthritis.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:13.000
All of these things that are done for our benefit anyway, and just in exchange for doing that, we get this unbelievable,

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:19.000
you know, this Paradise that, you know, is beyond our wildest dreams, and we know that it's even greater than this.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:24.000
Because this is just something that God gives us, which is to our limited ability to

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:29.000
to perceive anything. What God has in store for us is so much greater.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:34.000
In fact, we're told in the Quran that we can't even imagine what is in store for us

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:37.000
as a reward for doing what we're supposed to do in the first place.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:40.000
It's just incredible mercy.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:46.000
And, you know, we've talked about this before sometimes, well, you know.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:51.000
The Lower Heaven isn't that bad either, when we read the next verses you'll see, but

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:55.000
the picture here, I mean, there's not that great a differences that we know

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:58.000
that the Higher Heaven just means that we'll be closer to God.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:02.000
And that's the only understanding that we really need to have, is that we'll be closer to God.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:06.000
And the further away from Him we are, the more miserable we'll be.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:12.000
So, even though we'll be in Paradise in the Lower Heaven, it won't be the same.

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:17.000
And in the next verses, the Lower Heaven, starting with 62.

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:24.000
