Okay.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:34.000
We know...

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:35.000
Naghmeh: Really, should I repeat this?

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.000
Naghmeh: Oh, Okay.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:43.000
Okay, God says "and those who are far ahead will be far ahead."

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:46.000
And they will be closest to God.

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:48.000
And far ahead is, of course, the Highest Heaven.

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:57.000
Then, and we know that far ahead doesn't mean how much money you have or what looks you have

00:26:57.000 --> 00:27:00.000
or how much education you've got.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:07.000
But it means, what, the kind of intelligence that you have within where you see God and the truth and righteousness.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:15.000
And, and we know that that's what puts us far ahead.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:22.000
Not because, like I was saying earlier, that there are a lot of people who have all those things.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:25.000
And they feel like they have a lot of power and they're in control.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.000
But they are very miserable.

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:30.000
And they go through drugs and alcohol.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:37.000
Most of the people who are out there that are into drugs and alcohol are doctors, people that we go to help us,

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:42.000
people who make all that money and who are in the high parts of society.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
And people who think they are in control.

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:54.000
Not that every doctor is bad or anything like that. But the power has a lot of times led to trouble.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:58.000
Because people are not righteous enough. And they don't see.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:05.000
And they don't open their hearts. And they don't let go of that ego enough to understand that if you use your power with God's will,

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:09.000
then maybe you'll get somewhere. But other than that, you don't get anywhere.

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:17.000
Maybe here for a while. Like God says "I'll let them enjoy this life for a while." But just for a while.

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:22.000
And, then we know that there are people who don't have those things.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:28.000
Yet their lives are very calm and very fulfilled.

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:35.000
And also, as I was saying earlier, is that the Quran has taught us that God is in full control of our money, of what we look like,

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:42.000
of what we, of how our lives are the thread that we walk into our lives.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:51.000
And, then it seems pretty unfair that God would choose some people to have money and looks and put them in Heaven because of that.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:57.000
But what makes more sense is that God has given every one of us, no matter what standards we have,

00:28:57.000 --> 00:29:01.000
He has given us that freedom of choice, which makes us equal.

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:07.000
And makes us the wise ones if we seek to choose the right path.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:15.000
And, and that's where we'll be if we do the commandments in the Quran.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:23.000
If the people of Jesus or Moses' time did everything that they brought down through the Bible or the Torah.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:30.000
And, and if they did those things, then they will be in the Far Heaven.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.000
And of course we know that this is the most complete.

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:42.000
The prayers and the fasting and the charity, and belief in God alone and the Hereafter, and working righteousness.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:49.000
And, and God willing, that will put us far ahead and make us sovereigns on earth,

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.000
no matter how much money or anything we have.

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:56.000
And a lot of times I think that's really hard to understand.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
And a lot of times we get bogged down. I know I do.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Like when I see someone, you know, who has cute clothes on her, that's really pretty or something like that.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:12.000
And, and you just have to step back and think and say "that's not important. You have what God thought was good for you."

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:18.000
God says that you'll be

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:21.000
[56:12] In the gardens of bliss.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:25.000
[56:13] Multitudes from the early generations.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Gardens of bliss is of course Heaven.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.000
[56:13] Multitudes from the early generations.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:40.000
We have a footnote that says "the early generations of Muslims were characterized by following the Quran, the whole Quran, and nothing but the Quran.

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:48.000
250 years after the Prophet, Hadith and Sunnah appeared, followed by the various schools of jurisprudence.

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:53.000
This marked the progressive deterioration of the Muslim nation."

00:30:55.000 --> 00:31:04.000
Ok. This tells us "the early generations," those are the people that had the big prophets. Those are the ones who had the messengers

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:12.000
that... well, we have messengers, too, but it just seems like there then it seemed like it was more in people's lives.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:15.000
Now, it seems like technology has taken our lives so much that people don't think about

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:22.000
God actually sending angels down or messengers down or miracles down.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:33.000
But... So, those people who did follow the exact correct way were in the early generations and there are some people now.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:41.000
But right now it seems like we just need more and more and more proof to make us be disciplined enough to understand.

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:47.000
And, and it seems like as time has gone by, people just want to interpret the way they think.

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:51.000
They don't like something the way it sounds. They have to change it to the way they want it.

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:58.000
And that just makes a lot of conflict. And thank God that's why we have the Quran, which is so easy to understand.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:01.000
And God says it's easy to memorize and understand.

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:11.000
And, and it says in the footnote that "250 years after the Prophet, these two books appeared."

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:16.000
And we know that these two books are the books that have all the traditions, the things that are totally contradictory to the Quran.

00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:22.000
And these people are so blind that they don't even sit down to compare, to understand and see

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:28.000
that it is contradictory to what their Prophet that they idolize brought down.

00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:30.000
Number 14.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:34.000
[56:14] But only a few from the later generations.

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:42.000
And this again tells us that, you know, just the later it gets, the harder it is for people to understand and to follow.

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:53.000
And they're so bogged down by the material things of this life that it's too hard for them to be religious and to do five daily Prayers, and, or fast for a month.

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.000
They couldn't see that at all.

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:59.000
And, and so it seems like it is harder.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:07.000
And I guess now we have all the Prayer and we have all the five commandments.

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:13.000
And it is. It's more, I don't know what you wanna call it, technical or something to get.

00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:17.000
There's more work maybe to get to the Highest Heaven.

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:25.000
And it's harder for those people who wanna work that hard and wanna put in the time to do their Prayers and their fasting and wake up before dawn.

00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:34.000
And, and it is harder. And it just seems like those people have to go through more tests.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:40.000
And, and it just seems fair in that sense.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:43.000
God says, they will be

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.000
[56:15] On sturdy furnishings.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:47.000
They will relax in rows facing each other.

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:50.000
[56:17] Serving them will be immortal servants.

00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:52.000
[56:17] Serving them will be immortal servants.

00:33:53.000 --> 00:34:02.000
I know that a lot of these descriptions of the High Heaven or the Low Heaven, maybe even the Hell, they're all allegorical.

00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:12.000
And God is, knows us so well that He explains all these things to us in a way that we could understand.

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:19.000
And so everybody loves to relax and they love to have stable things around them.

00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:21.000
It seems like one day you're down and the next day you're up.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.000
But, God willing, in Heaven, everything will just be the same.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:30.000
And, and it says,

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.000
